# grep.chat - Project Information

This document provides a comprehensive overview of the grep.chat project architecture, stack, and patterns for AI assistants to understand the codebase.

---

## Project Overview

**grep.chat** is a production-grade, AI-powered chat application built with Next.js 15 that enables users to chat with multiple AI models via OpenRouter. It supports model selection, reasoning modes, web search, chat history persistence, and secure chat sharing.

---

## Technology Stack

### Core Framework

- **Next.js 15.5.4** (App Router, Turbopack, React Compiler)
- **React 19.1.1** (Server Components + Client Components)
- **TypeScript 5** (Strict mode enabled)

### AI & Chat

- **AI SDK** (`ai` v5.0.59, `@ai-sdk/react` v2.0.59) — Streaming chat with `useChat` hook
- **OpenRouter** (`@openrouter/ai-sdk-provider`) — Multi-model access (Claude, GPT-4, Gemini, DeepSeek, etc.)

### UI & Styling

- **Tailwind CSS v4** (`@tailwindcss/postcss`) — Utility-first styling
- **Radix UI** — Accessible primitive components (Dialog, Select, Dropdown, Tooltip, etc.)
- **shadcn/ui** — Component library built on Radix
- **Motion** (`motion/react`) — Animations with accessibility support
- **next-themes** — Dark/light theme management

### Backend & Database

- **Supabase** (`@supabase/ssr`, `@supabase/supabase-js`)
  - Authentication (OAuth with SSR cookies)
  - PostgreSQL with Row Level Security (RLS)
  - Real-time subscriptions
  - Generated TypeScript types
- **Redis** (`redis` v5.8.2) — Optional message caching with 24-hour TTL

### Content Rendering

- **react-markdown** — Markdown rendering in messages
- **shiki** — Syntax highlighting for code blocks
- **marked** — Markdown parsing
- **react-syntax-highlighter** — Alternative code block rendering

### Utilities

- **Zod** — Runtime validation and type safety
- **Sonner** — Toast notifications
- **cmdk** — Command palette (⌘K)
- **react-hotkeys-hook** — Keyboard shortcuts
- **uuid** — Chat ID generation

