## Architecture Patterns

### Routing (Next.js App Router)

- **File-based routing** with dynamic segments
  - `/` → New chat (generates UUID, redirects to `/chat/[id]`)
  - `/chat/[chatId]` → Existing chat (loads from database)
  - `/share/[chatId]` → Shared chat (read-only, public via share token)
- **Server Components by default**, Client Components with `"use client"`
- **Suspense boundaries** for loading states
- **Parallel routes** for modals/dialogs

### State Management

- **AI SDK hooks** (`useChat`) for chat state (messages, input, loading)
- **React Context** (`ChatsProvider`) for sidebar chat list
- **Server Actions** for data mutations (create, update, delete)
- **Local state** (`useState`, `useReducer`) for UI state
- **URL state** for navigation and deep linking

### API Design

#### RESTful API Routes

- `POST /api/chat` — Streaming chat endpoint
  - Validates user session
  - Handles message regeneration
  - Streams via OpenRouter with AI SDK
  - Supports reasoning modes & web search
  - Saves messages to Supabase on completion
- `DELETE /api/account` — Account deletion with cascade
- `GET /api/auth/callback` — OAuth callback handler

#### Server Actions (`"use server"`)

- `getMessagesByChatId(chatId)` — Fetch messages with Redis caching
- `ensureChat(chatId, title?, model?)` — Create or update chat
- `deleteChat(chatId)` — Delete chat and messages
- `getChatByShareToken(token)` — Fetch shared chat (public)
- `getUserChats()` — List user's chats

### Data Flow (Chat)

```
User Input → ChatInput Component
  ↓
useChat Hook (client-side state management)
  ↓
POST /api/chat (API Route with streaming)
  ↓
OpenRouter Provider → AI Model (Claude/GPT/etc.)
  ↓
Streaming Response → UI Update (real-time tokens)
  ↓
onFinish Callback → Save to Supabase
  ↓
Invalidate Redis Cache (messages:{chatId}{userId})
  ↓
Revalidate Path (/chat/[chatId])
```

### Authentication & Authorization

#### Supabase SSR Pattern

- **Cookie-based sessions** (no localStorage for security)
- **Middleware** refreshes session on every request
- **Server/Client separation**: Different Supabase clients for SSR
- **Service role** for admin operations (delete cascades, etc.)

#### Row Level Security (RLS)

All tables have RLS policies:

- **Users**: Can only read/update their own profile
- **Chats**: Can only access chats they own (user_id match)
- **Messages**: Can only access messages from their chats (via chat → user_id)

Security enforced at **database level**, not just application logic.

### Caching Strategy

#### Redis Caching

- **Purpose**: Reduce database load for frequently accessed messages
- **Cache Key**: `messages:{chatId}{userId}` (namespaced by user)
- **TTL**: 24 hours
- **Invalidation**: On message create/update/delete
- **Fallback**: Database if cache miss or Redis unavailable

#### Implementation

```typescript
// Cache read
const cached = await redis.get(`messages:${chatId}${userId}`);
if (cached) return JSON.parse(cached);

// Cache write
await redis.setex(`messages:${chatId}${userId}`, 86400, JSON.stringify(messages));

// Cache invalidation
await redis.del(`messages:${chatId}${userId}`);
```

