## Security Considerations

### Authentication

- ✅ Supabase SSR with httpOnly cookies
- ✅ Session refresh in middleware
- ✅ OAuth providers (GitHub, Google, etc.)
- ✅ No tokens in localStorage (XSS protection)

### Authorization

- ✅ RLS policies on all tables
- ✅ User can only access their own data
- ✅ Service role key server-only (never exposed)
- ✅ Session validation on all API routes

### API Security

- ✅ CSRF protection via Supabase SSR
- ✅ Input validation with Zod
- ✅ Rate limiting (recommended to add)
- ✅ Environment variable separation (public/private)

### Data Privacy

- ✅ Share tokens for public access (no chat ID exposure)
- ✅ Cascade deletes on account deletion
- ✅ No PII in logs or error messages

